From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: koalabuttz <27229333+koalabuttz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 04:21:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] security: bound server fastfile references by the array size

FS_ServerSetReferencedFFs passed 1024 as the capacity of
fs_serverReferencedFFNames and fs_serverReferencedFFCheckSums, which
hold 32 entries each. A server that lists more than 32 fastfiles made
the client write past both arrays.

Pass the array size.
---
 src/qcommon/files.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/qcommon/files.cpp b/src/qcommon/files.cpp
index 67e28798..84c7b20e 100644
--- a/src/qcommon/files.cpp
+++ b/src/qcommon/files.cpp
@@ -353,7 +353,7 @@ void __cdecl FS_ServerSetReferencedFFs(char *FFSums, char *FFNames)
     fs_numServerReferencedFFs = FS_ServerSetReferencedFiles(
         FFSums,
         FFNames,
-        1024,
+        ARRAY_COUNT(fs_serverReferencedFFNames),
         fs_serverReferencedFFCheckSums,
         fs_serverReferencedFFNames);
 }
